        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(compaction): avoid cached usage overcount",
        "body": "﻿Closes #99843AI-assisted: Codex.## What Problem This SolvesFixes an issue where long cached Anthropic agent turns could auto-compact far below the configured reserve threshold when the persisted final assistant usage had `totalTokens` missing or zero. In that state, repeated `cacheRead`/`cacheWrite` billing buckets could be summed as if they were one live context-window snapshot, so sessions compacted early and displayed a misleadingly huge token count.## Why This Change Was MadeThe final assistant-message path now carries the latest streamed positive usage `total` onto a cached final usage snapshot when the final message already has provider usage buckets but lacks a trusted `totalTokens`. That preserves the provider's final billing buckets while restoring the real per-call context snapshot needed by compaction. The compaction estimator was simplified back to the canonical rule: use positive `totalTokens` when present, otherwise fall back to the usage buckets for callers that only have a single-call usage snapshot.## User ImpactUsers running long cached tool-loop sessions should no longer see safeguard compaction fire early just because cached prompt billing buckets were counted repeatedly across calls. Sessions with a real cached context above the reserve threshold still compact, because the streamed total is preserved before the estimator reads the assistant message.## Evidence- Current PR head: `f38d6681d51bef4050e4cc5cc4cf09ffdbdd57c5`.- Redacted packaged-session terminal transcript using production `preservePendingAssistantUsage`, real `SessionManager` session-file append/reopen, `buildSessionContext`, `estimateContextTokens`, `calculateContextTokens`, and `shouldCompact`:```console$ node --import tsx %TEMP%/openclaw-99843-packaged-session-proof.ts{\"label\":\"issue-99843-packaged-session\",\"sessionFile\":\"<redacted-temp-session.jsonl>\",\"total\":163978,\"messageCount\":3,\"persistedTotalTokens\":163978,\"persistedCacheRead\":819661,\"persistedCacheWrite\":93130,\"directContextTokens\":163978,\"trailingTokens\":3225,\"estimatedTokens\":167203,\"threshold\":180000,\"shouldCompact\":false}{\"label\":\"above-threshold-packaged-session\",\"sessionFile\":\"<redacted-temp-session.jsonl>\",\"total\":190000,\"messageCount\":3,\"persistedTotalTokens\":190000,\"persistedCacheRead\":819661,\"persistedCacheWrite\":93130,\"directContextTokens\":190000,\"trailingTokens\":3225,\"estimatedTokens\":193225,\"threshold\":180000,\"shouldCompact\":true}```- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compaction.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 --reporter=dot` -> 1 file, 6 tests passed.- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-core.config.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.messages.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 --reporter=dot` -> 1 file, 44 tests passed.- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compaction.ts packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compaction.test.ts packages/agent-core/src/harness/agent-harness.ts src/agents/sessions/agent-session.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.messages.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.messages.test.ts` -> passed.- `git diff --check -- packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compaction.ts packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compaction.test.ts packages/agent-core/src/harness/agent-harness.ts src/agents/sessions/agent-session.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.messages.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.messages.test.ts` -> passed.- CI on `f38d6681d51bef4050e4cc5cc4cf09ffdbdd57c5` passed the relevant gates, including `check-prod-types`, `check-test-types`, `check-lint`, `Critical Quality (agent-runtime-boundary)`, `Real behavior proof`, `QA Smoke CI`, and all `checks-node-compact-*` shards.",
